---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Download a backup by its key from `backup ls`; a gzip board file.
The file goes to ~/Downloads unless a file is given; `holst b import` reads it.

USAGE
  holst backup get <key> [<file>] [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  key    The backup's key from `holst backup ls`
  file   A new file, never overwritten, - for stdout; ~/Downloads by default

FLAGS
  --provider provider   Where the server keeps the backup, as `backup ls` shows; the usual place by default
  --no-compress         Save without gzip, which adds .gz to the file name

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst backup get 1761552000
  $ holst backup get 1761552000 roadmap.ydoc --no-compress

LEARN MORE
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
